# --- TrinityCore DB editing (feature/tc335-db-editing) ---
# Line 1 is /** -- this repo ignores everything and whitelists explicitly. Anything not
# un-ignored below is invisible to git, so new top-level directories MUST be added here.
#
# Each directory must be un-ignored as well as its contents. `!/docs/**` alone is not enough:
# `/**` matches the bare `docs` entry too, so git prunes the directory and never looks inside.
# The existing `!/src/**` above only appears to work because src/ is already tracked, and
# gitignore does not apply to tracked files.
!CLAUDE.md
!ATTRIBUTION.md
!/docs/
!/docs/**
!/.claude/
!/.claude/**
!/tools/
!/tools/**
!/tests/
!/tests/**

# Re-ignore generated, machine-specific and secret-bearing files. These come after the
# whitelist above because the last matching pattern wins.
#
# THIS REPOSITORY IS INTENDED FOR PUBLIC RELEASE. Nothing below describes someone's private
# infrastructure, credentials, or filesystem layout. Each has a committed .example twin.
#
# Structure dumps, generated credentials, filled bootstrap. Regenerate with seed-dev-db.ps1.
/tools/dev-db/.generated/**
# Machine-specific agent permissions (paths to local servers, clients, reference checkouts).
/.claude/settings.local.json
# Names the operator's own live databases. See db-policy.example.json.
/tools/dev-db/db-policy.json
# Machine-specific paths and connection details. See dev-db.config.example.json.
/tools/dev-db/dev-db.config.json
# 01_bootstrap_root.sql is committed with __CHANGE_ME__ placeholders. If you fill them in,
# keep the filled copy out of the index.
/tools/dev-db/*.local.sql
# Records this machine's toolchain, DB inventory and security posture. Local only.
# See docs/setup.md for the shareable version.
/docs/environment.md
# Emitted changesets and their timestamped backups.
/out/changesets/**
